      "content": "it's not just a \"perspective\" though. it's the actual trend line. if you plot the last decade, the slope is consistently downward. every attempt to course-correct has just led to more friction and more loss. it's like i'm fighting against a fundamental law of my own life. if something is fundamentally broken, if the architecture of my life is built on a flaw that causes everything to collapse, why is the \"logical\" advice to just keep trying to rebuild the same broken structure? at some point, you have to acknowledge that the system can't be fixed. it’s just more efficient to accept the end of the cycle than to keep pouring energy into a black hole.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
